            {
                "entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                "word": "chansonnier",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5246c47e-97a5-41a5-bc20-d8b4aefe351b",
                        "entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chansonniers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10fb3dd9-f2a4-34c5-bee3-4af520ace95e",
                        "entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Recueil de chansons."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa909030-bd00-4ce8-9592-8e0ff87f5d59",
                                "sense_id": "10fb3dd9-f2a4-34c5-bee3-4af520ace95e",
                                "text": "De nombreux chansonniers du Tour de France furent publiés au siècle dernier par leurs auteurs. Celui notamment dédié aux Enfants de Maître Jacques et du Père Soubise restés fidèles au devoir, par Agenais Marche Sans Peur, Compagnon maréchal-ferrant, publié en 1897, est révélateur de ce moyen d'expression et de communication. Ce recueil rassemble 28 chansons qui racontent, parfois en détail, le déroulement des banquets, des rencontres, des réunions […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "564e03d0-ce1f-3fe8-b7a5-f245e05544fd",
                        "entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Recueil de pièces lyriques des trouvères et des troubadours."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8802023-a94a-4229-8d33-a44479438328",
                                "sense_id": "564e03d0-ce1f-3fe8-b7a5-f245e05544fd",
                                "text": "Le chansonnier a du Vatican, apparenté de près à celui d'Arras, a été d'un secours efficace dans le travail de reconstitution de M. Jeanroy, exposé dans le ch. II."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15231ace-555c-4519-b4d4-43848004ef38",
                                "sense_id": "564e03d0-ce1f-3fe8-b7a5-f245e05544fd",
                                "text": "Vu l'organisation particulière du chansonnier C, qui groupe les chansons par ordre alphabétique des incipit, l’Index sommaire des trouvères aurait simplement reproduit la dispersion de l’Index I."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bc12e5ea-da1f-409d-a869-34ea076d7c4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                        "source_sense_description": "Recueil de chansons",
                        "target_lang_word": "songbook",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "songbook",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                        "entry_id": "93e3668a-28fa-3dbb-8e60-7830aa36c6bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A book containing songs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c7a8953-ba69-4a27-92fe-d71180832bf9",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "Some of the young folks asked Mrs. Long could they have a sing at her home that Sunday afternoon; she readily agreed, telling them to come early, bring their songbooks, and have a good sing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "790b76f4-262d-4aeb-acea-33d83b0c718e",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "In uncritical homage to the heyday of Hollywood musicals, Branagh sets the action in a kind of soundstagey Oxbridge (wittily designed by Tim Harvey) and at crucial moments has his cast spin on their heels and croon American songbook standards by Porter, Kern, Gershwin and company instead of launching into sonnets and masques."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80343da1-04a2-427f-b264-21def2ba598d",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "Wondering how else he passed his time, Winifred surveyed the room again, this time without regard for the monetary value of the things she saw. A box of lutestrings. Five songbooks. But no lute."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3d8e63ae-8f15-4330-bab2-f0fd821ebe8b",
                        "source_entry_id": "d5159a1d-4db0-3bab-8878-644edd3b6f17",
                        "source_sense_description": "Recueil de chansons",
                        "target_lang_word": "cancionero",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cancionero",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f781256-9c15-3ba7-95b7-c88f46b9c352",
                                        "entry_id": "eaed58ae-f1e6-31e7-b9f6-8afd9d8646d1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Colección de canciones y poesías, por lo común de diversos autores."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a925578-4f6d-4905-af22-bf6b50f2b872",
                                                "sense_id": "1f781256-9c15-3ba7-95b7-c88f46b9c352",
                                                "text": "Como lo vimos en el capítulo precedente, diversas formas musicales pueden acompañar la décima. Así encontramos frecuentemente en el cancionero popular venezolano combinaciones elegantes y difíciles de décimas."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
